"""Regime carrier rows of the class-A line (n+d, n, n+1), every gap d >= d0.

Generated by `kernel/class_a_gap_regimes.mojo fit 1 <labels> 5 16 5 5 ...` from the exact label
datasets of evidence/class-a-gap-labels-2026-10-23/: for each residue regime, one
l-affine table shared by every gap from its floor. A proof *target*: evidence only
through `psc.class_a_gap_uniform.certify_regime_closure`. `regimes()` lists
`[eps, kind, j, j1, d0, l_fit]` (kind 0 low r=j, 1 high r=d-j, 2 middle j<=r<=d-j1).
Source note: docs/class-a-gap-uniform-certificate-design-2026-10-23.md.
"""


def regimes_plus() -> List[List[Int]]:
    return List[List[Int]]([
        List[Int]([1, 0, 0, 0, 5, 5]),
        List[Int]([1, 0, 1, 0, 7, 5]),
        List[Int]([1, 0, 2, 0, 8, 5]),
        List[Int]([1, 0, 3, 0, 9, 5]),
        List[Int]([1, 0, 4, 0, 10, 5]),
        List[Int]([1, 1, 1, 0, 5, 5]),
        List[Int]([1, 1, 2, 0, 5, 5]),
        List[Int]([1, 1, 3, 0, 6, 5]),
        List[Int]([1, 1, 4, 0, 8, 5]),
        List[Int]([1, 1, 5, 0, 9, 5]),
        List[Int]([1, 2, 5, 6, 11, 5]),
    ])


